{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rubied-nonvagrant-whimbrel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`terraform plan` cannot run at all against `infra/terraform`. Every terraform operation on this\nbox is blocked — not just the change that discovered it.\n\n    Error in function call\n      on main.tf line 63: user_data = templatefile(\"${path.module}/user_data.sh\", {...})\n    Call to function \"templatefile\" failed: ./user_data.sh:92,24-25: Invalid character;\n    This character is not used within the language., and 3 other diagnostic(s).\n\n## Root cause\n\nMerged commit `ef1a7e66a65d` (\"Gate standalone shell scripts with ShellCheck\") added explanatory\nCOMMENTS to `infra/terraform/user_data.sh`. Each escapes the FIRST mention of a bash brace\nexpansion as `$${...}` but leaves the 'reduces to' / 'becomes' half UNESCAPED. Three sites, all\ninside `#` comments:\n\n- `:92`  — `# reduces to ${!PARAMS[@]} / ${PARAMS[$name]}. ...`\n- `:111` — `# After rendering, \"$${!PARAMS[@]}\" becomes \"${!PARAMS[@]}\" ...`\n\nHarmless to bash — a comment is a comment. Fatal to `templatefile()`, which interpolates the\nWHOLE file regardless of shell comment syntax and tries to evaluate `${!PARAMS[@]}` as HCL.\n\n## Why this is P1\n\nIt blocks ALL terraform work on this box, not one ticket. `-target` does not help: terraform\nevaluates the entire configuration before honouring `-target`, so a plan restricted to four SSM\nparameters fails identically. There is no narrow path around it.\n\nDiscovered while attempting the `terraform apply` that `colourless-hasteless-lamb` needs. That\nchange (`0f1d0cfc7792`) does NOT touch `user_data.sh` — the file is byte-identical to\n`origin/main`, so this is pre-existing and independent.\n\n## Established while diagnosing (useful for whoever fixes it)\n\n- State is REMOTE: S3 `rebar-tfstate-896586841071`, key `rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate`,\n  us-east-1, `encrypt = true`, `use_lockfile = true` (no DynamoDB table).\n- `terraform init` SUCCEEDS and providers resolve; local CLI 1.15.8 clears the `>= 1.10` floor\n  that `use_lockfile` silently requires. So the break is purely the template evaluation.\n- When fixed, the change plans as an IN-PLACE update: `user_data_replace_on_change` defaults to\n  `false`, so correcting the comments does NOT rebuild the Gerrit box. Worth stating, because\n  'terraform wants to change user_data' reads alarming otherwise.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `terraform plan` runs to completion against `infra/terraform`.\n- [ ] The three comment sites escape BOTH halves (`$$`), or the comments are reworded to avoid\n      the sequence entirely.\n- [ ] A guard rejects an unescaped `${` in any file consumed by `templatefile()`, so a future\n      comment cannot silently break every terraform operation again. ShellCheck cannot catch this\n      — the file is valid bash; the breakage is in a different consumer.\n- [ ] LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE: a real `terraform plan` output recorded in a comment,\n      showing it completes.\n\n## Note\n\nThe agent that found this deliberately did NOT edit `user_data.sh` to unblock itself: it is an\nunrelated file that feeds production `user_data`, and it belongs in its own reviewed change.\nThat was the right call.","id":"dd30-f10d-69f3-4c36","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["terraform","infra","blocker","iac"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"terraform plan/apply is BROKEN on main: unescaped ${...} in user_data.sh comments breaks templatefile()"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787868647534036001,"uuid":"90fbc7fe-600e-4a48-843a-812d90459e40"}